What changed:
- packages/modules/ar: BatchPreview gains `status` (preview/approved/posted/cancelled);
  loadBatchPreview reads it, a new preview is 'preview'.
- apps/api GET /ar/batches/:id, POST preview and approve now return `status`, per item
  `status`, `invoice_no`, `failure_code`, `failure_message` (from batchSummary) and
  `outcome {posted, failed, posted_gross}`. Additive; approve still returns status 'approved'.
- New api-db test SS-UC02-08 (December batch, one party archived before the run).

Why: the batch screen (SS-UC02-08) must show the exception list after the job ran and must not
offer Approve on a batch that is already approved; the read route had neither.

Validation:
- RED first: `pnpm exec vitest run --project api-db apps/api/src/ar/batches.db.test.ts`
  failed on `status` undefined (.agent/evidence/T-0084/red-api-batch-status-20261113.txt).
- GREEN: same file 6/6; `vitest run --project db packages/modules/ar/src/batch` 8/8.
- eslint + prettier on touched files clean. Typecheck not yet run.

Next action: Playwright spec tests/e2e/web/batch-billing.spec.ts (RED), then the screens.

